{% comment %}
  pricing-estimate.liquid — derived from order-confirmation-receipt.liquid.

  The ONLY structural change is the item table: instead of one row per piece with
  weights and taxable columns, each piece opens into its price components —
  gold, diamonds, coloured stones, making — each with the weight it was priced
  on and the rate it was quoted at. Everything else (masthead, addresses,
  post-tax adjustments, amount in words, terms) is the order confirmation's,
  unchanged. It carries NO payment or balance rows: this document quotes a
  price, it does not track what has been paid against it.

  This is a QUOTE, shared with the customer for approval before they commit. It
  is not a tax document: no HSN, no GST breakup, no place of supply.

  ── Where the numbers come from ──────────────────────────────────────────────
  Every figure is a LINE ITEM PROPERTY, falling back to the variant or product
  metafield behind it. That matters for Order Printer: line item properties
  travel on the line item itself, so unlike order metafields they are always
  readable at print time.

  Four rates are STORED, not derived — the middleware writes each one only when
  that rate genuinely produced the value:
    _gold_rate      per gram, locked on the line at reprice
    _making_rate    per gram, falling back to product custom.making_charges_rate.
                    Blank when a flat custom.making override set the labour, so
                    no rate is shown that was never quoted.
    _gemstone_rate  per carat, from product custom.gemstone_price
  Only the diamond per-carat rate is derived (Diamond / _diamond_cts), and it is
  suppressed when quantity > 1, because money properties are line totals while
  carat properties are per piece.

  Gemstone became a first-class component on 2026-09-04 (server.js). A draft
  created before that deploy carries no Gemstone property until it is edited or
  repriced — the variant metafield fallback below covers it either way.

  NOTE: keep angle brackets out of these comments. Order Printer validates the
  template as HTML and reads them as unknown tags, rejecting the paste.
{% endcomment %}
<style>
  @page { size: A4; margin: 0.5cm; }
  * { margin: 0; padding: 0; box-sizing: border-box; }
  @media print {
    body { padding: 5px !important; margin: 0; }
    .container { page-break-inside: avoid !important; }
    a { display: none !important; visibility: hidden !important; }
  }
  body { font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 8px; line-height: 1.2; padding: 10px; }
  .container { max-width: 800px; margin: 0 auto; border: 2px solid #000; padding: 0; }
  .header-text { text-align: right; padding: 3px 8px; font-size: 7px; font-style: italic; border-bottom: 1px solid #000; }
  .title-header { text-align: center; padding: 7px 10px; border-bottom: 2px solid #000; min-height: 60px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; justify-content: center; align-items: center; }
  .logo { max-width: 120px; height: auto; margin-bottom: 4px; }
  .title-center h1 { font-size: 14px; font-weight: bold; margin: 0; }
  .company-invoice-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1.5fr 1fr; border-bottom: 2px solid #000; }
  .company-section { padding: 5px 8px; border-right: 2px solid #000; font-size: 7px; line-height: 1.35; }
  .company-section strong { font-size: 7.5px; }
  .invoice-details-grid { display: grid; grid-template-rows: repeat(3, 1fr); }
  .invoice-detail-row { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr 1fr; border-bottom: 1px solid #000; }
  .invoice-detail-row:last-child { border-bottom: none; }
  .invoice-detail-cell { padding: 4px 6px; font-size: 7px; border-right: 1px solid #000; }
  .invoice-detail-cell:last-child { border-right: none; }
  .invoice-detail-cell strong { display: block; font-size: 7px; font-weight: bold; margin-bottom: 1px; }
  .addresses-section { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; border-bottom: 2px solid #000; }
  .address-block { padding: 5px 8px; font-size: 7px; line-height: 1.3; }
  .address-block:first-child { border-right: 2px solid #000; }
  .address-block strong { display: block; margin-bottom: 1px; font-size: 7px; }
  .address-field { margin-bottom: 2px; }
  table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; }
  .items-table { font-size: 7px; }
  .items-table th { background-color: #f0f0f0; padding: 3px 4px; text-align: left; font-weight: bold; border: 1px solid #000; font-size: 7px; line-height: 1.2; }
  .items-table td { padding: 3px 4px; border: 1px solid #000; vertical-align: top; }
  .items-table .text-right { text-align: right; }
  .items-table .text-center { text-align: center; }
  {% comment %}── Breakdown rows. The piece header separates one item from the next; component
  rows are indented under it so the eye reads them as parts of that piece. ──{% endcomment %}
  .piece-row td { background-color: #f7f7f7; font-weight: bold; font-size: 7.5px; }
  .piece-row .piece-sub { font-weight: normal; font-size: 6.5px; color: #555; }
  .component-row .component-label { padding-left: 14px; }
  .component-row .qualifier { color: #666; font-size: 6.5px; font-style: italic; }
  .discount-row td { color: #7a1f1f; }
  .item-total-row td { font-weight: bold; background-color: #efefef; font-size: 7.5px; }
  .totals-row td { font-weight: normal; padding: 3px 4px; font-size: 7px; }
  .total-row td { font-weight: bold; font-size: 8px; background-color: #f9f9f9; }
  .tbd { color: #999; font-style: italic; }
  .amount-words { padding: 4px 8px; font-size: 7px; font-weight: bold; border-top: 2px solid #000; display: flex; justify-content: space-between; }
  .footer-section { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; border-top: 2px solid #000; font-size: 6.5px; line-height: 1.25; }
  .footer-left { padding: 6px 8px; border-right: 2px solid #000; }
  .footer-right { padding: 6px 8px; }
  .footer-left h3, .footer-right h3 { font-size: 7px; margin-bottom: 3px; font-weight: bold; }
  .footer-left p, .footer-right p { margin-bottom: 2px; }
  .watermark { position: relative; }
  .watermark-image { position: absolute; top: 50%; left: 50%; transform: translate(-50%, -50%); opacity: 0.08; width: 200px; height: auto; z-index: 0; pointer-events: none; }
</style>


{% comment %}══ Gold rate, and the day it was locked ════════════════════════════════════════
Scanned up here rather than in the footer: an estimate is only as good as the rate it
quotes, so the rate and its date belong at the top beside the validity window. Same
18kt/14kt cross-derivation the other documents use.
──{% endcomment %}
{% assign rate_18k = "" %}
{% assign rate_14k = "" %}
{% assign gold_updated = "" %}
{% for line_item in order.line_items %}
  {% assign sku_parts = line_item.variant.sku | split: "|" %}
  {% assign karat = sku_parts[2] | strip %}
  {% assign locked_rate = "" %}
  {% assign locked_ts   = "" %}
  {% for p in line_item.properties %}
    {% if p.first == "_gold_rate"       %}{% assign locked_rate = p.last %}{% endif %}
    {% if p.first == "_gold_updated_at" %}{% assign locked_ts   = p.last %}{% endif %}
  {% endfor %}
  {% if karat == "18" and rate_18k == "" and locked_rate != "" %}{% assign rate_18k = locked_rate %}{% if locked_ts != "" %}{% assign gold_updated = locked_ts %}{% endif %}{% endif %}
  {% if karat == "14" and rate_14k == "" and locked_rate != "" %}{% assign rate_14k = locked_rate %}{% if gold_updated == "" and locked_ts != "" %}{% assign gold_updated = locked_ts %}{% endif %}{% endif %}
{% endfor %}
{% if rate_18k == "" and rate_14k != "" %}{% assign rate_18k = rate_14k | plus: 0 | times: 0.771 | divided_by: 0.604 | round: 2 %}{% endif %}
{% if rate_14k == "" and rate_18k != "" %}{% assign rate_14k = rate_18k | plus: 0 | times: 0.604 | divided_by: 0.771 | round: 2 %}{% endif %}

<div class="container">

  <div class="header-text">Pricing Estimate — not a tax invoice</div>

  <div class="title-header">
    <img src="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0775/8322/0993/files/Timanti_Logo_Black.jpg?v=1766506323" alt="Timanti Logo" class="logo">
    <div class="title-center"><h1>Pricing Estimate</h1></div>
  </div>

  <div class="company-invoice-grid">
    <div class="company-section">
      <strong>AURACARAT PRIVATE LIMITED</strong><br>
      <strong>Address:</strong> C207 Crystal Plaza, New Link Road, Andheri (W), Mumbai – 400053 Maharashtra<br>
      <strong>Store Address:</strong> 17th Cross, 19th Main Rd, HSR Layout Sec 2, Opp. Gnan Srishti School, Bengaluru – 560102<br>
      <strong>Tel:</strong> +91-7710938305 &nbsp;|&nbsp; <strong>Email:</strong> hello@timanti.in &nbsp;|&nbsp; <strong>Website:</strong> www.timanti.in<br>
      <strong>GSTIN</strong> – 29ABBCA3309B1Z7 &nbsp;|&nbsp; <strong>PAN</strong> – ABBCA3309B
    </div>

    <div class="invoice-details-grid">
      <div class="invoice-detail-row">
        <div class="invoice-detail-cell">
          <strong>Estimate No.</strong>{{ order.name }}
        </div>
        <div class="invoice-detail-cell">
          <strong>Estimate Date</strong>{{ order.created_at | date: "%d/%m/%Y" }}
        </div>
        <div class="invoice-detail-cell">
          {% comment %}Seven days from the estimate, because the gold rate below moves daily.{% endcomment %}
          <strong>Valid Until</strong>{{ order.created_at | date: "%s" | plus: 604800 | date: "%d/%m/%Y" }}
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="invoice-detail-row">
        <div class="invoice-detail-cell">
          <strong>Gold Rate 18kt</strong>{% if rate_18k != "" %}₹{{ rate_18k }} /g{% else %}<span class="tbd">—</span>{% endif %}
        </div>
        <div class="invoice-detail-cell">
          <strong>Gold Rate 14kt</strong>{% if rate_14k != "" %}₹{{ rate_14k }} /g{% else %}<span class="tbd">—</span>{% endif %}
        </div>
        <div class="invoice-detail-cell">
          <strong>Rate As Of</strong>{% if gold_updated != "" %}{% assign ist_ts = gold_updated | date: "%s" | plus: 19800 %}{{ ist_ts | date: "%d %b %Y" }}{% else %}{{ order.created_at | date: "%d %b %Y" }}{% endif %}
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="invoice-detail-row">
        <div class="invoice-detail-cell" style="grid-column: 1 / -1; font-size: 6px; word-break: break-all;">
          <strong>SKU Code</strong>
          {% for line_item in order.line_items %}{{ line_item.sku }}{% unless forloop.last %}<br>{% endunless %}{% endfor %}
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="addresses-section">
    <div class="address-block">
      <strong>Prepared For:</strong>
      {% assign ba = order.billing_address %}
      {% if ba %}
        <div class="address-field"><strong>Customer Name:</strong> {{ ba.first_name | upcase }} {{ ba.last_name | upcase }}</div>
        <div class="address-field"><strong>Address:</strong> {{ ba.address1 }}{% if ba.address2 %}, {{ ba.address2 }}{% endif %}, {{ ba.city }}, {{ ba.province }}{% if ba.zip %} – {{ ba.zip }}{% endif %}, {{ ba.country }}</div>
        <div class="address-field"><strong>Mobile:</strong> {{ ba.phone }}</div>
        <div class="address-field"><strong>Email:</strong> {{ order.email }}</div>
      {% endif %}
    </div>
    <div class="address-block">
      <strong>Delivery To:</strong>
      {% assign sa = order.shipping_address %}
      {% if sa %}
        <div class="address-field"><strong>Customer Name:</strong> {{ sa.first_name | upcase }} {{ sa.last_name | upcase }}</div>
        <div class="address-field"><strong>Address:</strong> {{ sa.address1 }}{% if sa.address2 %}, {{ sa.address2 }}{% endif %}, {{ sa.city }}, {{ sa.province }}{% if sa.zip %} – {{ sa.zip }}{% endif %}, {{ sa.country }}</div>
        <div class="address-field"><strong>Mobile:</strong> {{ sa.phone }}</div>
        <div class="address-field"><strong>Email:</strong> {{ order.email }}</div>
      {% endif %}
    </div>
  </div>

  <table class="items-table">
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th style="width: 44%;">Price Component</th>
        <th class="text-center" style="width: 16%;">Weight</th>
        <th class="text-right" style="width: 18%;">Rate</th>
        <th class="text-right" style="width: 22%;">Value</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody class="watermark">
      <img src="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0775/8322/0993/files/Timanti_Logo_Black.jpg?v=1766506323" alt="Watermark" class="watermark-image">

      {% assign order_total_rs = 0 %}
      {% assign piece_no = 0 %}

      {% for line_item in order.line_items %}

        {% comment %}── Product lines only. An exchange note reaches the draft as a negative custom
        line and a manual discount as a negative-priced line; neither is a piece, and breaking
        either one into components would print an empty block. Both are handled in the totals
        section below, exactly as the order confirmation handles them. ──{% endcomment %}
        {% assign li_title = line_item.title | downcase %}
        {% assign skip_line = false %}
        {% if li_title contains "exchange note" %}{% assign skip_line = true %}{% endif %}
        {% if li_title contains "discount" and line_item.price < 0 %}{% assign skip_line = true %}{% endif %}

        {% unless skip_line %}
        {% assign piece_no = piece_no | plus: 1 %}

        {% assign qty = line_item.quantity | plus: 0 %}
        {% if qty < 1 %}{% assign qty = 1 %}{% endif %}

        {% comment %}══ Read every property once ═════════════════════════════════════════════
        Component VALUES are stored as "Rs44103.00" and are LINE TOTALS (already times
        quantity). Weights and carats are PER PIECE. Rates are stored bare.
        ──{% endcomment %}
        {% assign v_gold = "" %}{% assign v_dia = "" %}{% assign v_making = "" %}{% assign v_gem = "" %}
        {% assign v_dia_ad = "" %}{% assign v_making_ad = "" %}
        {% assign v_taxable = "" %}{% assign v_gst = "" %}{% assign v_disc = "0" %}
        {% assign w_net = "" %}{% assign w_gross = "" %}{% assign c_dia = "" %}{% assign n_dia = "" %}{% assign c_gem = "" %}
        {% assign r_gold = "" %}{% assign r_making = "" %}{% assign r_gem = "" %}{% assign jcode = "" %}
        {% for p in line_item.properties %}
          {% if p.first == "Gold"                    %}{% assign v_gold      = p.last | remove: "Rs" | strip %}{% endif %}
          {% if p.first == "Diamond"                 %}{% assign v_dia       = p.last | remove: "Rs" | strip %}{% endif %}
          {% if p.first == "Gemstone"                %}{% assign v_gem       = p.last | remove: "Rs" | strip %}{% endif %}
          {% if p.first == "Making" or p.first == "Making Charges" %}{% assign v_making = p.last | remove: "Rs" | strip %}{% endif %}
          {% if p.first == "Diamond (After Discount)" %}{% assign v_dia_ad    = p.last | remove: "Rs" | strip %}{% endif %}
          {% if p.first == "Making (After Discount)"  %}{% assign v_making_ad = p.last | remove: "Rs" | strip %}{% endif %}
          {% if p.first == "Taxable Value"           %}{% assign v_taxable   = p.last | remove: "Rs" | strip %}{% endif %}
          {% if p.first == "GST"                     %}{% assign v_gst       = p.last | remove: "Rs" | strip %}{% endif %}
          {% if p.first == "Discount Applied"        %}{% assign v_disc      = p.last | remove: "Rs" | strip %}{% endif %}
          {% if p.first == "_net_wt"                 %}{% assign w_net       = p.last | strip %}{% endif %}
          {% if p.first == "_gross_wt"               %}{% assign w_gross     = p.last | strip %}{% endif %}
          {% if p.first == "_diamond_cts"            %}{% assign c_dia       = p.last | strip %}{% endif %}
          {% if p.first == "_diamond_pcs"            %}{% assign n_dia       = p.last | strip %}{% endif %}
          {% if p.first == "_gemstone_cts"           %}{% assign c_gem       = p.last | strip %}{% endif %}
          {% if p.first == "_gold_rate"              %}{% assign r_gold      = p.last | strip %}{% endif %}
          {% if p.first == "_making_rate"            %}{% assign r_making    = p.last | strip %}{% endif %}
          {% if p.first == "_gemstone_rate"          %}{% assign r_gem       = p.last | strip %}{% endif %}
          {% if p.first == "_jewel_code"             %}{% assign jcode       = p.last | strip %}{% endif %}
        {% endfor %}

        {% comment %}── Fallbacks: every chain ends at the variant or product metafield the
        catalogue actually holds. Variant breakups are PER UNIT, so they are multiplied by
        quantity to match the line-total convention of the properties above. ──{% endcomment %}
        {% if v_gold   == "" and line_item.variant.metafields.custom.price_breakup_gold    %}{% assign v_gold   = line_item.variant.metafields.custom.price_breakup_gold    | times: qty %}{% endif %}
        {% if v_dia    == "" and line_item.variant.metafields.custom.price_breakup_diamond %}{% assign v_dia    = line_item.variant.metafields.custom.price_breakup_diamond | times: qty %}{% endif %}
        {% if v_making == "" and line_item.variant.metafields.custom.price_breakup_making  %}{% assign v_making = line_item.variant.metafields.custom.price_breakup_making  | times: qty %}{% endif %}
        {% comment %}Gemstone value became a line item property on 2026-09-04. Older drafts have
        none, so the variant metafield the catalogue prices from is read directly.{% endcomment %}
        {% if v_gem    == "" and line_item.variant.metafields.custom.gemstone_charges      %}{% assign v_gem    = line_item.variant.metafields.custom.gemstone_charges      | times: qty %}{% endif %}

        {% if w_net  == "" and line_item.variant.metafields.custom.net_metal_weight_g   %}{% assign w_net  = line_item.variant.metafields.custom.net_metal_weight_g   %}{% endif %}
        {% if w_net  == "" and line_item.product.metafields.custom.net_metal_weight_g   %}{% assign w_net  = line_item.product.metafields.custom.net_metal_weight_g   %}{% endif %}
        {% if w_gross == "" and line_item.variant.metafields.custom.gross_weight_g      %}{% assign w_gross = line_item.variant.metafields.custom.gross_weight_g      %}{% endif %}
        {% if c_dia  == "" and line_item.product.metafields.custom.totaldiamondweight   %}{% assign c_dia  = line_item.product.metafields.custom.totaldiamondweight   %}{% endif %}
        {% if c_dia  == "" and line_item.variant.metafields.custom.totaldiamondweight   %}{% assign c_dia  = line_item.variant.metafields.custom.totaldiamondweight   %}{% endif %}
        {% if n_dia  == "" and line_item.product.metafields.custom.diamond_pcs          %}{% assign n_dia  = line_item.product.metafields.custom.diamond_pcs          %}{% endif %}
        {% if n_dia  == "" and line_item.product.metafields.custom.totaldiamondcount    %}{% assign n_dia  = line_item.product.metafields.custom.totaldiamondcount    %}{% endif %}
        {% if c_gem  == "" and line_item.product.metafields.custom.gemstone_weight      %}{% assign c_gem  = line_item.product.metafields.custom.gemstone_weight      %}{% endif %}
        {% if r_gold == "" and line_item.variant.metafields.custom.gold_rate            %}{% assign r_gold = line_item.variant.metafields.custom.gold_rate            %}{% endif %}
        {% comment %}The two product rates. custom.making_charges_rate is the quoted labour rate per
        gram and custom.gemstone_price the quoted stone rate per carat — both live on the PRODUCT,
        the values they produce on the variant. The rate column is left blank when neither the line
        nor the product carries a rate, which is the case when a flat custom.making override set the
        labour: the amount is then simply what was agreed, and there is no per-gram rate to show.{% endcomment %}
        {% if r_making == "" and line_item.product.metafields.custom.making_charges_rate %}{% assign r_making = line_item.product.metafields.custom.making_charges_rate %}{% endif %}
        {% if r_gem  == "" and line_item.product.metafields.custom.gemstone_price       %}{% assign r_gem  = line_item.product.metafields.custom.gemstone_price       %}{% endif %}

        {% comment %}times: 1.0 rather than plus: 0 throughout — Liquid does INTEGER division when
        both operands are integers, so a value like "61920" over carats "1" would silently truncate
        the per-carat rate. Forcing every operand to a float makes the arithmetic exact.{% endcomment %}
        {% assign n_gold   = v_gold   | times: 1.0 %}
        {% assign n_dia_v  = v_dia    | times: 1.0 %}
        {% assign n_mk     = v_making | times: 1.0 %}
        {% assign n_gem_v  = v_gem    | times: 1.0 %}
        {% assign n_disc   = v_disc   | times: 1.0 %}
        {% assign subtotal = n_gold | plus: n_dia_v | plus: n_mk | plus: n_gem_v %}

        {% comment %}── Metal, from the variant title: "18K / YG / 18"" reads as 18K Yellow Gold ──{% endcomment %}
        {% assign vt = line_item.variant_title | split: " / " %}
        {% assign metal_karat = vt[0] | strip %}
        {% assign metal_tone = "" %}
        {% if vt[1] %}
          {% assign tone_code = vt[1] | strip | upcase %}
          {% if tone_code == "YG" %}{% assign metal_tone = "Yellow Gold" %}
          {% elsif tone_code == "WG" %}{% assign metal_tone = "White Gold" %}
          {% elsif tone_code == "RG" %}{% assign metal_tone = "Rose Gold" %}
          {% else %}{% assign metal_tone = tone_code %}{% endif %}
        {% endif %}

        {% comment %}══ Piece header ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════{% endcomment %}
        {% comment %}line_item.title already reads "Product Title - 18K / YG / 14" in Order Printer,
        so printing it AND variant_title spelled the options out twice. product.title is the clean
        name; the options are appended once, with the gross weight inside the same brackets rather
        than floating in a column of its own.{% endcomment %}
        {% assign piece_title = line_item.product.title | default: line_item.title %}
        <tr class="piece-row">
          <td colspan="4">
            {{ piece_no }}. {{ piece_title }}{% if line_item.variant_title != blank or w_gross != "" %} ({% if line_item.variant_title != blank %}{{ line_item.variant_title }}{% endif %}{% if line_item.variant_title != blank and w_gross != "" %}, {% endif %}{% if w_gross != "" %}{{ w_gross | plus: 0 | round: 3 }} g gross{% endif %}){% endif %}
            <span class="piece-sub">
              {% if jcode != "" %}&nbsp;·&nbsp;{{ jcode }}{% endif %}
              {% if qty > 1 %}&nbsp;·&nbsp;Qty {{ qty }}{% endif %}
            </span>
          </td>
        </tr>

        {% comment %}── Gold. Weight and rate are both stored, so nothing here is derived. On a
        multi-piece line the weight is shown as "2 × 4.820 g" — the rate is per gram of one
        piece, and the value covers them all. ──{% endcomment %}
        {% if n_gold > 0 %}
          <tr class="component-row">
            <td class="component-label">
              Gold{% if metal_karat != blank %} — {{ metal_karat }}{% if metal_tone != "" %} {{ metal_tone }}{% endif %}{% endif %}
            </td>
            <td class="text-center">
              {% if w_net != "" %}{% if qty > 1 %}{{ qty }} &times; {% endif %}{{ w_net | plus: 0 | round: 3 }} g <span class="qualifier">net</span>{% else %}<span class="tbd">TBC</span>{% endif %}
            </td>
            <td class="text-right">{% if r_gold != "" %}₹{{ r_gold | plus: 0 | times: 100 | round | money_without_currency | remove: ',' }} /g{% else %}—{% endif %}</td>
            <td class="text-right">₹{{ n_gold | times: 100 | round | money_without_currency | remove: ',' }}</td>
          </tr>
        {% endif %}

        {% comment %}── Diamonds. Pieces, carats and value — no rate. The per-carat figure used to be
        derived here as value ÷ carats, and it is deliberately gone: a parcel is not priced at one
        flat rate per carat, so a derived number invites the customer to multiply it back out and
        arrive at a price we never quoted. Coloured stones below keep their rate, which is the
        product's own stored custom.gemstone_price — quoted, not reverse-engineered. ──{% endcomment %}
        {% if n_dia_v > 0 %}
          <tr class="component-row">
            <td class="component-label">
              Diamonds{% if n_dia != "" and n_dia != "0" %} — {{ n_dia }} pcs{% endif %}
            </td>
            <td class="text-center">
              {% if c_dia != "" and c_dia != "0.00" %}{{ c_dia | plus: 0 | round: 3 }} ct{% else %}<span class="tbd">TBC</span>{% endif %}
            </td>
            <td class="text-right">—</td>
            <td class="text-right">₹{{ n_dia_v | times: 100 | round | money_without_currency | remove: ',' }}</td>
          </tr>
        {% endif %}

        {% comment %}── Coloured stones. Priced as a component in its own right since 2026-09-04;
        the rate is the product's own custom.gemstone_price, never the diamond rate. The whole
        row disappears on a piece with no coloured stones. ──{% endcomment %}
        {% if n_gem_v > 0 %}
          <tr class="component-row">
            <td class="component-label">Coloured stones</td>
            <td class="text-center">
              {% if c_gem != "" and c_gem != "0.00" %}{{ c_gem | plus: 0 | round: 3 }} ct{% else %}<span class="tbd">TBC</span>{% endif %}
            </td>
            <td class="text-right">{% if r_gem != "" %}₹{{ r_gem | plus: 0 | times: 100 | round | money_without_currency | remove: ',' }} /ct{% else %}—{% endif %}</td>
            <td class="text-right">₹{{ n_gem_v | times: 100 | round | money_without_currency | remove: ',' }}</td>
          </tr>
        {% endif %}

        {% comment %}── Making. A rate prints only when _making_rate is on the line, which the
        middleware writes only when a per-gram rate actually produced the value. Labour agreed as
        a flat amount shows its value and a dash — never a rate reverse-engineered from it. ──{% endcomment %}
        {% if n_mk > 0 %}
          <tr class="component-row">
            <td class="component-label">
              Making charges
            </td>
            <td class="text-center">
              {% if w_net != "" %}{% if qty > 1 %}{{ qty }} &times; {% endif %}{{ w_net | plus: 0 | round: 3 }} g{% else %}—{% endif %}
            </td>
            <td class="text-right">{% if r_making != "" %}₹{{ r_making | plus: 0 | times: 100 | round | money_without_currency | remove: ',' }} /g{% endif %}</td>
            <td class="text-right">₹{{ n_mk | times: 100 | round | money_without_currency | remove: ',' }}</td>
          </tr>
        {% endif %}

        {% comment %}══ Discount, split by what it landed on ═══════════════════════════════════
        A per-line discount stacks across three targets at once — diamond, making and the whole
        line — and they are summed into one "Discount Applied". The split is recoverable only by
        subtraction: each after-discount property is the component minus the cut that targeted it,
        so whatever the two do not explain was a discount on the line as a whole.

        When neither after-discount property is present (a line last touched by the manual reprice
        endpoint, which does not write them) there is nothing to attribute, so a single unlabelled
        Discount row prints instead of guessing a target.
        ──{% endcomment %}
        {% assign disc_dia = 0 %}
        {% assign disc_mk  = 0 %}
        {% assign has_split = false %}
        {% if v_dia_ad != "" %}
          {% assign has_split = true %}
          {% assign disc_dia = n_dia_v | minus: v_dia_ad %}
          {% if disc_dia < 0.01 %}{% assign disc_dia = 0 %}{% endif %}
        {% endif %}
        {% if v_making_ad != "" %}
          {% assign has_split = true %}
          {% assign disc_mk = n_mk | minus: v_making_ad %}
          {% if disc_mk < 0.01 %}{% assign disc_mk = 0 %}{% endif %}
        {% endif %}
        {% assign disc_rest = n_disc | minus: disc_dia | minus: disc_mk %}
        {% if disc_rest < 0.01 %}{% assign disc_rest = 0 %}{% endif %}

        {% if disc_dia > 0 %}
          <tr class="component-row discount-row">
            <td class="component-label">Less: Discount on diamonds</td>
            <td class="text-center">—</td>
            <td class="text-right">—</td>
            <td class="text-right">− ₹{{ disc_dia | times: 100 | round | money_without_currency | remove: ',' }}</td>
          </tr>
        {% endif %}
        {% if disc_mk > 0 %}
          <tr class="component-row discount-row">
            <td class="component-label">Less: Discount on making</td>
            <td class="text-center">—</td>
            <td class="text-right">—</td>
            <td class="text-right">− ₹{{ disc_mk | times: 100 | round | money_without_currency | remove: ',' }}</td>
          </tr>
        {% endif %}
        {% if disc_rest > 0 %}
          <tr class="component-row discount-row">
            <td class="component-label">Less: Discount{% if has_split %} on order value{% endif %}</td>
            <td class="text-center">—</td>
            <td class="text-right">—</td>
            <td class="text-right">− ₹{{ disc_rest | times: 100 | round | money_without_currency | remove: ',' }}</td>
          </tr>
        {% endif %}

        {% comment %}══ Taxable, GST, item total ═══════════════════════════════════════════════
        Taxable Value is read DIRECTLY, never re-derived from Gross Value. Gross Value means
        pre-discount on a line the reprice engine wrote and post-discount on one the manual
        endpoint wrote, so dividing it and subtracting the discount would double-count that
        discount on the manual lines. Taxable Value carries the same meaning in every path.
        ──{% endcomment %}
        {% assign taxable = 0 %}
        {% if v_taxable != "" %}
          {% assign taxable = v_taxable | times: 1.0 %}
        {% else %}
          {% assign taxable = subtotal | minus: n_disc %}
        {% endif %}
        {% if taxable < 0 %}{% assign taxable = 0 %}{% endif %}

        {% assign gst = 0 %}
        {% if v_gst != "" %}
          {% assign gst = v_gst | times: 1.0 %}
        {% else %}
          {% assign gst = taxable | times: 0.03 %}
        {% endif %}

        {% comment %}Accumulated but NOT printed per piece. Each piece closes on its GST line; the
        only total on the document is the order's, so the estimate reads as one price made of parts
        rather than a stack of sub-invoices. The order total is still the sum of Taxable + GST across
        the pieces, so it ties to the rows above it.{% endcomment %}
        {% assign item_total = taxable | plus: gst %}
        {% assign order_total_rs = order_total_rs | plus: item_total %}

        {% comment %}A product line the pricing engine has never touched carries no components and
        no Taxable Value. Say so rather than printing a silent zero — staff need to know to reprice
        before this reaches a customer.{% endcomment %}
        {% if subtotal <= 0 and taxable <= 0 %}
          <tr class="component-row">
            <td colspan="4" class="text-center tbd">Pricing for this piece is not yet finalised.</td>
          </tr>
        {% else %}
          <tr class="component-row">
            <td colspan="3" class="text-right">Taxable value</td>
            <td class="text-right">₹{{ taxable | times: 100 | round | money_without_currency | remove: ',' }}</td>
          </tr>
          <tr class="component-row">
            <td colspan="3" class="text-right">GST @ 3%</td>
            <td class="text-right">₹{{ gst | times: 100 | round | money_without_currency | remove: ',' }}</td>
          </tr>
          <tr class="item-total-row">
            <td colspan="3" class="text-right">Item {{ piece_no }} total (incl. GST)</td>
            <td class="text-right">₹{{ item_total | times: 100 | round | money_without_currency | remove: ',' }}</td>
          </tr>
        {% endif %}

        {% endunless %}
      {% endfor %}

      {% comment %}══ Order totals ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
      Summed from the item totals above, which are themselves Taxable + GST — so the estimate
      total always ties to the sum of its own rows.
      ──{% endcomment %}
      {% assign estimate_total = order_total_rs | times: 100 | round %}

      <tr class="total-row">
        <td colspan="3" class="text-right"><strong>Total Estimate Value (incl. GST)</strong></td>
        <td class="text-right"><strong>₹{{ estimate_total | money_without_currency | remove: ',' }}</strong></td>
      </tr>

      {% assign final_payable = estimate_total %}

      {% comment %}══ Post-tax adjustments ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════
      Verbatim from the order confirmation: metafield first, note attribute as the fallback for
      when Order Printer resolves no metafields at print time. These are the only deductions that
      happen AFTER the 3% — everything inside a line is already net of its discounts.
      ──{% endcomment %}
      {% assign og_value  = order.metafields.custom.old_gold_value.value  | default: order.metafields.custom.old_gold_value  | plus: 0 %}
      {% assign og_weight = order.metafields.custom.old_gold_weight.value | default: order.metafields.custom.old_gold_weight | plus: 0 %}
      {% assign og_karat  = order.metafields.custom.old_gold_purity.value | default: order.metafields.custom.old_gold_purity | default: "" %}
      {% for attr in order.note_attributes %}
        {% if attr.name == "old_gold_value"  and og_value  == 0 %}{% assign og_value  = attr.value | plus: 0 %}{% endif %}
        {% if attr.name == "old_gold_weight" and og_weight == 0 %}{% assign og_weight = attr.value | plus: 0 %}{% endif %}
        {% if attr.name == "old_gold_purity" and og_karat  == "" %}{% assign og_karat  = attr.value %}{% endif %}
        {% if attr.name == "old_gold_karat"  and og_karat  == "" %}{% assign og_karat  = attr.value %}{% endif %}
      {% endfor %}
      {% if og_value > 0 %}
        {% assign og_value_paise = og_value | times: 100 | round %}
        <tr class="totals-row">
          <td colspan="3" class="text-right" style="border-top: 1px solid #ccc;">Less: Consideration against Gold received ({{ og_weight }}g{% if og_karat != "" %}, {{ og_karat }}kt{% endif %})</td>
          <td class="text-right" style="border-top: 1px solid #ccc;">− ₹{{ og_value_paise | money_without_currency | remove: ',' }}</td>
        </tr>
        {% assign final_payable = final_payable | minus: og_value_paise %}
      {% endif %}

      {% assign exc_value = order.metafields.custom.exchange_note_value.value | default: order.metafields.custom.exchange_note_value | plus: 0 %}
      {% for attr in order.note_attributes %}
        {% if attr.name == "exchange_note_value" and exc_value == 0 %}{% assign exc_value = attr.value | plus: 0 %}{% endif %}
      {% endfor %}
      {% if exc_value > 0 %}
        {% assign exc_value_paise = exc_value | times: 100 | round %}
        <tr class="totals-row">
          <td colspan="3" class="text-right" style="border-top: 1px solid #ccc;">Less: Exchange Note Adjustment</td>
          <td class="text-right" style="border-top: 1px solid #ccc;">− ₹{{ exc_value_paise | money_without_currency | remove: ',' }}</td>
        </tr>
        {% assign final_payable = final_payable | minus: exc_value_paise %}
      {% endif %}

      {% assign voucher_value = order.metafields.custom.voucher_value.value | default: order.metafields.custom.voucher_value | plus: 0 %}
      {% assign voucher_code  = "" %}
      {% for attr in order.note_attributes %}
        {% if attr.name == "voucher_value" and voucher_value == 0 %}{% assign voucher_value = attr.value | plus: 0 %}{% endif %}
      {% endfor %}
      {% for tag in order.tags %}
        {% assign _t = tag | strip %}
        {% if _t contains "voucher-num:" %}{% assign voucher_code = _t | remove: "voucher-num:" | strip %}{% endif %}
      {% endfor %}
      {% if voucher_value > 0 %}
        {% assign voucher_value_paise = voucher_value | times: 100 | round %}
        <tr class="totals-row">
          <td colspan="3" class="text-right" style="border-top: 1px solid #ccc;">Less: Voucher Adjustment{% if voucher_code != "" %} ({{ voucher_code }}){% endif %}</td>
          <td class="text-right" style="border-top: 1px solid #ccc;">− ₹{{ voucher_value_paise | money_without_currency | remove: ',' }}</td>
        </tr>
        {% assign final_payable = final_payable | minus: voucher_value_paise %}
      {% endif %}

      {% if og_value > 0 or exc_value > 0 or voucher_value > 0 %}
        {% if final_payable < 0 %}{% assign final_payable = 0 %}{% endif %}
        <tr class="total-row">
          <td colspan="3" class="text-right"><strong>Net Payable</strong></td>
          <td class="text-right"><strong>₹{{ final_payable | money_without_currency | remove: ',' }}</strong></td>
        </tr>
      {% endif %}

      {% comment %}══ Money already taken against this draft ═════════════════════════════════
      Up to four installment legs and up to two refunds, read exactly the way the tax invoice
      reads them: the flat installment_N / refund_N metafields first, then the i1: to i4: and
      r1: to r2: tags for when Order Printer hands this template empty order.metafields at print
      time. The middleware writes both onto the DRAFT on every recompute, so an estimate the
      customer has already paid against can show what has moved.

      Legs are stored in RUPEES. Every other figure in this totals block is PAISE, so each leg is
      scaled by 100 before it meets final_payable.

      A cad_advance leg prints as Design Advance and counts as money paid, exactly as on the
      invoice — it is settled against this order either way.

      Balance Pending is measured against final_payable, not against the gross estimate value: the
      gold, exchange and voucher adjustments above have already reduced what is owed, and the
      balance has to be the number the customer would actually hand over.

      NOTE: keep angle brackets out of this comment. Order Printer validates the template as HTML
      and reads them as unknown tags, rejecting the paste with "Tag value invalid".
      ──{% endcomment %}
      {% assign inst_rows = "" %}
      {% for i in (1..4) %}
        {% case i %}
          {% when 1 %}
            {% assign _v = order.metafields.custom.installment_1_value.value | default: order.metafields.custom.installment_1_value | plus: 0 %}
            {% assign _m = order.metafields.custom.installment_1_mode.value  | default: order.metafields.custom.installment_1_mode  | append: "" %}
            {% assign _d = order.metafields.custom.installment_1_date.value  | default: order.metafields.custom.installment_1_date  | append: "" %}
            {% assign _t = order.metafields.custom.installment_1_type.value  | default: order.metafields.custom.installment_1_type  | append: "" %}
          {% when 2 %}
            {% assign _v = order.metafields.custom.installment_2_value.value | default: order.metafields.custom.installment_2_value | plus: 0 %}
            {% assign _m = order.metafields.custom.installment_2_mode.value  | default: order.metafields.custom.installment_2_mode  | append: "" %}
            {% assign _d = order.metafields.custom.installment_2_date.value  | default: order.metafields.custom.installment_2_date  | append: "" %}
            {% assign _t = "" %}
          {% when 3 %}
            {% assign _v = order.metafields.custom.installment_3_value.value | default: order.metafields.custom.installment_3_value | plus: 0 %}
            {% assign _m = order.metafields.custom.installment_3_mode.value  | default: order.metafields.custom.installment_3_mode  | append: "" %}
            {% assign _d = order.metafields.custom.installment_3_date.value  | default: order.metafields.custom.installment_3_date  | append: "" %}
            {% assign _t = "" %}
          {% when 4 %}
            {% assign _v = order.metafields.custom.installment_4_value.value | default: order.metafields.custom.installment_4_value | plus: 0 %}
            {% assign _m = order.metafields.custom.installment_4_mode.value  | default: order.metafields.custom.installment_4_mode  | append: "" %}
            {% assign _d = order.metafields.custom.installment_4_date.value  | default: order.metafields.custom.installment_4_date  | append: "" %}
            {% assign _t = "" %}
        {% endcase %}
        {% if _v > 0 %}
          {% assign inst_rows = inst_rows | append: _d | append: "|" | append: _m | append: "|" | append: _v | append: "|" | append: _t | append: "~" %}
        {% endif %}
      {% endfor %}
      {% if inst_rows == "" %}
        {% for i in (1..4) %}
          {% assign pfx = "i" | append: i | append: ":" %}
          {% for tg in order.tags %}
            {% assign t = tg | strip %}
            {% if t contains pfx %}
              {% assign pp = t | remove_first: pfx | split: "@" %}
              {% assign _v = pp[0] | plus: 0 %}
              {% if _v > 0 %}
                {% assign _m = pp[1] | default: "" %}
                {% assign _d = pp[2] | default: "" %}
                {% assign _t = "" %}
                {% if pp[3] == "c" %}{% assign _t = "cad_advance" %}{% endif %}
                {% assign inst_rows = inst_rows | append: _d | append: "|" | append: _m | append: "|" | append: _v | append: "|" | append: _t | append: "~" %}
              {% endif %}
            {% endif %}
          {% endfor %}
        {% endfor %}
      {% endif %}
      {% assign inst_list = inst_rows | split: "~" %}

      {% assign refund_rows = "" %}
      {% for i in (1..2) %}
        {% case i %}
          {% when 1 %}
            {% assign _rv = order.metafields.custom.refund_1_value.value | default: order.metafields.custom.refund_1_value | plus: 0 %}
            {% assign _rm = order.metafields.custom.refund_1_mode.value  | default: order.metafields.custom.refund_1_mode  | append: "" %}
            {% assign _rd = order.metafields.custom.refund_1_date.value  | default: order.metafields.custom.refund_1_date  | append: "" %}
          {% when 2 %}
            {% assign _rv = order.metafields.custom.refund_2_value.value | default: order.metafields.custom.refund_2_value | plus: 0 %}
            {% assign _rm = order.metafields.custom.refund_2_mode.value  | default: order.metafields.custom.refund_2_mode  | append: "" %}
            {% assign _rd = order.metafields.custom.refund_2_date.value  | default: order.metafields.custom.refund_2_date  | append: "" %}
        {% endcase %}
        {% if _rv > 0 %}
          {% assign refund_rows = refund_rows | append: _rd | append: "|" | append: _rm | append: "|" | append: _rv | append: "~" %}
        {% endif %}
      {% endfor %}
      {% if refund_rows == "" %}
        {% for i in (1..2) %}
          {% assign rpfx = "r" | append: i | append: ":" %}
          {% for tg in order.tags %}
            {% assign t = tg | strip %}
            {% if t contains rpfx %}
              {% assign rp = t | remove_first: rpfx | split: "@" %}
              {% assign _rv = rp[0] | plus: 0 %}
              {% if _rv > 0 %}
                {% assign _rm = rp[1] | default: "" %}
                {% assign _rd = rp[2] | default: "" %}
                {% assign refund_rows = refund_rows | append: _rd | append: "|" | append: _rm | append: "|" | append: _rv | append: "~" %}
              {% endif %}
            {% endif %}
          {% endfor %}
        {% endfor %}
      {% endif %}
      {% assign refund_list = refund_rows | split: "~" %}

      {% if inst_list.size > 0 or refund_list.size > 0 %}
        {% assign paid_paise = 0 %}
        {% for row in inst_list %}
          {% assign pay_c = row | split: "|" %}
          {% assign leg_paise = pay_c[2] | plus: 0 | times: 100 | round %}
          {% assign paid_paise = paid_paise | plus: leg_paise %}
          <tr class="totals-row">
            <td colspan="3" class="text-right"{% if forloop.first %} style="border-top: 1px solid #ccc;"{% endif %}>
              {% if pay_c[3] == "cad_advance" %}Design Advance{% else %}Amount Paid{% endif %}
              {% if pay_c[0] != "" %}&nbsp;<em style="color:#555;">{{ pay_c[0] | date: "%d %b %Y" }}</em>{% endif %}
              {% if pay_c[1] != "" %}&nbsp;<em style="color:#555;">({{ pay_c[1] }})</em>{% endif %}
            </td>
            <td class="text-right"{% if forloop.first %} style="border-top: 1px solid #ccc;"{% endif %}>₹{{ leg_paise | money_without_currency | remove: ',' }}</td>
          </tr>
        {% endfor %}

        {% comment %}A refund reverses a PAYMENT. It never reduces the quoted price, so it sits
        here among the money rows and not with the adjustments above.{% endcomment %}
        {% for row in refund_list %}
          {% assign pay_r = row | split: "|" %}
          {% assign ref_paise = pay_r[2] | plus: 0 | times: 100 | round %}
          {% assign paid_paise = paid_paise | minus: ref_paise %}
          <tr class="totals-row">
            <td colspan="3" class="text-right"{% if forloop.first and inst_list.size == 0 %} style="border-top: 1px solid #ccc;"{% endif %}>
              Less: Refund
              {% if pay_r[0] != "" %}&nbsp;<em style="color:#555;">{{ pay_r[0] | date: "%d %b %Y" }}</em>{% endif %}
              {% if pay_r[1] != "" %}&nbsp;<em style="color:#555;">({{ pay_r[1] }})</em>{% endif %}
            </td>
            <td class="text-right"{% if forloop.first and inst_list.size == 0 %} style="border-top: 1px solid #ccc;"{% endif %}>− ₹{{ ref_paise | money_without_currency | remove: ',' }}</td>
          </tr>
        {% endfor %}

        {% comment %}The net only earns a row when more than one thing moved — against a single
        payment and no refund it would simply restate the row above it.{% endcomment %}
        {% assign money_rows = inst_list.size | plus: refund_list.size %}
        {% if money_rows > 1 %}
          <tr class="totals-row">
            <td colspan="3" class="text-right">Net Amount Paid</td>
            <td class="text-right">₹{{ paid_paise | money_without_currency | remove: ',' }}</td>
          </tr>
        {% endif %}

        {% comment %}Clamped at zero: money taken past the estimate is an excess to be settled when
        the piece is billed, not a negative balance on a document that quotes a price.{% endcomment %}
        {% assign balance_pending = final_payable | minus: paid_paise %}
        {% if balance_pending < 0 %}{% assign balance_pending = 0 %}{% endif %}
        <tr class="total-row">
          <td colspan="3" class="text-right"><strong>Balance Pending</strong></td>
          <td class="text-right"><strong>₹{{ balance_pending | money_without_currency | remove: ',' }}</strong></td>
        </tr>
      {% endif %}
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <div style="padding: 4px 10px; font-size: 7.5px; font-style: italic; border-top: 1px solid #ccc;">
    Weights, stone counts and prices shown are indicative estimates against the gold rate quoted above. Final weights and price will be confirmed on the tax invoice at the time of dispatch.
  </div>

  <div class="amount-words">
    <span>
      {% assign ones = "Zero,One,Two,Three,Four,Five,Six,Seven,Eight,Nine,Ten,Eleven,Twelve,Thirteen,Fourteen,Fifteen,Sixteen,Seventeen,Eighteen,Nineteen" | split: "," %}
      {% assign tens = "Zero,Ten,Twenty,Thirty,Forty,Fifty,Sixty,Seventy,Eighty,Ninety" | split: "," %}
      {% assign total_int = final_payable | divided_by: 100 | floor %}
      {% assign words = "" %}
      {% assign crores = total_int | divided_by: 10000000 %}
      {% if crores > 0 %}{% assign temp = crores | modulo: 100 %}{% if temp < 20 %}{% assign words = words | append: ones[temp] | append: " " %}{% else %}{% assign td = temp | divided_by: 10 %}{% assign od = temp | modulo: 10 %}{% assign words = words | append: tens[td] %}{% if od > 0 %}{% assign words = words | append: "-" | append: ones[od] %}{% endif %}{% assign words = words | append: " " %}{% endif %}{% assign words = words | append: "Crore " %}{% assign total_int = total_int | modulo: 10000000 %}{% endif %}
      {% assign lakhs = total_int | divided_by: 100000 %}
      {% if lakhs > 0 %}{% assign temp = lakhs | modulo: 100 %}{% if temp < 20 %}{% assign words = words | append: ones[temp] | append: " " %}{% else %}{% assign td = temp | divided_by: 10 %}{% assign od = temp | modulo: 10 %}{% assign words = words | append: tens[td] %}{% if od > 0 %}{% assign words = words | append: "-" | append: ones[od] %}{% endif %}{% assign words = words | append: " " %}{% endif %}{% assign words = words | append: "Lakh " %}{% assign total_int = total_int | modulo: 100000 %}{% endif %}
      {% assign thousands = total_int | divided_by: 1000 %}
      {% if thousands > 0 %}{% assign temp = thousands | modulo: 100 %}{% if temp < 20 %}{% assign words = words | append: ones[temp] | append: " " %}{% else %}{% assign td = temp | divided_by: 10 %}{% assign od = temp | modulo: 10 %}{% assign words = words | append: tens[td] %}{% if od > 0 %}{% assign words = words | append: "-" | append: ones[od] %}{% endif %}{% assign words = words | append: " " %}{% endif %}{% assign words = words | append: "Thousand " %}{% assign total_int = total_int | modulo: 1000 %}{% endif %}
      {% assign hundreds = total_int | divided_by: 100 %}{% if hundreds > 0 %}{% assign words = words | append: ones[hundreds] | append: " Hundred " %}{% assign total_int = total_int | modulo: 100 %}{% endif %}
      {% if total_int > 0 %}{% if total_int < 20 %}{% assign words = words | append: ones[total_int] %}{% else %}{% assign td = total_int | divided_by: 10 %}{% assign od = total_int | modulo: 10 %}{% assign words = words | append: tens[td] %}{% if od > 0 %}{% assign words = words | append: "-" | append: ones[od] %}{% endif %}{% endif %}{% endif %}
      Amount in Words: Rupees {{ words }} Only
    </span>
    <span>E. &amp; O. E.</span>
  </div>

  <div class="footer-section">
    <div class="footer-left">
      <h3>Terms of this Estimate</h3>
      <p>
        <strong>1.</strong> This is a pricing estimate issued for approval. It is not a tax invoice, not a demand for payment, and creates no obligation on either party until the order is confirmed.<br>
        <strong>2.</strong> Prices are quoted against the gold rate stated above. Gold rates move daily; a change in the rate revises this estimate.<br>
        <strong>3.</strong> Weights, stone counts and carat weights are the design specification. Actual weights are confirmed after production and the final price is billed on the tax invoice.<br>
